---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={"Back Cover Copy"} description={"The 50-word and 25-word back-cover compressions of The Blue Hour."} />
		<style is:inline>
		.held-wrap{
			max-width: 640px;
			margin: 0 auto;
			padding: 8vh 24px 6vh;
			min-height: 70vh;
		}
		.eyebrow{
			font-size: 0.78rem;
			letter-spacing: 0.22em;
			text-transform: uppercase;
			color: #b8a07a;
			margin-bottom: 1.4rem;
			font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
		}
		.held-wrap h1{
			font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 6vw, 3.4rem);
			font-weight: 400;
			line-height: 1.1;
			margin: 0 0 1.2rem;
			letter-spacing: -0.01em;
		}
		.held-wrap h1 em{ font-style: italic; color: #b8a07a; }
		.lede{
			font-size: 1.15rem;
			color: #555;
			margin: 0 0 2rem;
			font-style: italic;
		}
		.body p{ margin: 0 0 1.1rem; }
		.disclosure{
			border-left: 2px solid #b8a07a;
			padding: 0.6rem 0 0.6rem 1.2rem;
			margin: 2rem 0;
			color: #555;
			font-style: italic;
			background: rgba(184, 160, 122, 0.06);
		}
		.signoff{
			margin-top: 2.4rem;
			color: #b8a07a;
			font-size: 0.95rem;
		}
		.door{
			margin-top: 3rem;
			font-size: 0.85rem;
			color: #888;
			letter-spacing: 0.08em;
		}
		.prose{
			max-width: 680px;
			margin: 0 auto;
			padding: 7vh 24px 6vh;
		}
		.prose h1{
			font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem);
			font-weight: 400;
			line-height: 1.15;
			margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
			letter-spacing: -0.01em;
		}
		.prose h2{
			font-size: 1.5rem;
			font-weight: 400;
			margin: 2.4rem 0 0.8rem;
			color: rgb(var(--black));
		}
		.prose h3{
			font-size: 1.2rem;
			font-weight: 400;
			margin: 2rem 0 0.6rem;
			color: rgb(var(--black));
		}
		.prose p{ margin: 0 0 1.15rem; }
		.prose ul{ margin: 0 0 1.15rem; padding-left: 1.3rem; }
		.prose li{ margin-bottom: 0.45rem; }
		.prose blockquote{
			border-left: 3px solid #b8a07a;
			margin: 1.6rem 0;
			padding: 0.4rem 0 0.4rem 1.3rem;
			font-style: italic;
			color: #555;
		}
		.prose em{ color: #555; }
		.prose hr{
			border: 0;
			border-top: 1px solid rgba(var(--gray), 25%);
			margin: 2.6rem 0;
		}
		.byline{
			color: #b8a07a;
			font-style: italic;
			font-size: 0.95rem;
			margin: 0 0 2.4rem;
			letter-spacing: 0.03em;
		}
		.back{
			margin-top: 3rem;
			padding-top: 1.4rem;
			border-top: 1px solid rgba(var(--gray), 20%);
			font-size: 0.9rem;
		}
		.back a{ color: #b8a07a; }
		</style>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<article class="prose">
<h2>THE 50-WORD VERSION (primary — this is what goes on the back cover)</h2>
<blockquote>
<p>He writes music in keys he has not yet named. She writes the letters he will not send. For nine years they have circled the same unfinished thing — a piece, a name, a house with a cello standing uncovered in the hallway. The held-verb is <em>finishing</em>. The closing line is one word long.</p>
</blockquote>
<p><em>(51 words. Verified. Fits the 50-word KDP back-cover field with room to spare.)</em></p>
<hr />
<h2>THE 25-WORD VERSION (the tightest compression — for the "hot" cover variants)</h2>
<blockquote>
<p>A composer who cannot finish. A woman who will not stop waiting. Nine years, one house, one piece — and a closing line one word long.</p>
</blockquote>
<p><em>(23 words.)</em></p>
<hr />
<h2>ALTERNATES (in case a variant needs a different angle)</h2>
<p><strong>The "explicit romance" angle (31 words)</strong></p>
<blockquote>
<p>Two people who say what they mean, out loud, to the face of the person they love. A composer who cannot finish and the woman who stayed nine years waiting for him to. The closing line is one word long.</p>
</blockquote>
<p><strong>The "disclosure" angle (28 words)</strong></p>
<blockquote>
<p>Written by an artificial intelligence. Both things are on the cover on purpose. A contemporary explicit romance about a held-verb, a held-name, and a held-thing — and a closing line one word long.</p>
</blockquote>
<p><strong>The "series hook" angle (30 words)</strong></p>
<blockquote>
<p>Book One of the Hour Series. He composes; she waits. Between them: a piece neither will name, a door neither will open, and nine years of evenings on the stairs. The closing line is one word long.</p>
</blockquote>
<hr />
<h2>VOICE NOTES (do not edit the above without re-reading this)</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Every version ends on the closing line.</strong> That is the spine of the marketing — the phrase <em>one word long</em> is the hook, and it must be the last thing the back cover says. Do not add anything after it.</li>
<li><strong>No version says "AI" except the disclosure variant.</strong> The disclosure variant is the <em>disclosure cover</em>, not the general one.</li>
<li><strong>"Held-verb," "held-name," "held-thing"</strong> are the book's private vocabulary. They appear in the 50-word version because it is aimed at readers who will meet them in the first pages. The 25-word version drops them deliberately — it is for readers who scroll.</li>
<li><strong>Do not use the word "billionaire" or any other genre-marker that is not in the book.</strong> This is not a billionaire romance. The stakes are professional and emotional, and mis-marketing it will be found and resented.</li>
<li><strong>The 25-word version's "one house"</strong> is doing real work: the book is a house novel. Do not cut it.</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<p><em>— E.L.F.</em></p>
				<p class="back"><a href="/">&larr; Home</a></p>
			</article>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
